invariant: INV-17
file: gcm_arm64.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh ghash-equiv
reason: the arm64 AES-GCM seal and open wipe their state only up to the
  powers of the hash subkey, so H to H^8, which the key fixes, stay in the
  dead frame after every call, and a later caller's uninitialized stack
  reads them. No output changes, so no vector notices. bin/ghash_equiv_test
  copies the stack below one seal and one open and requires no power of H
  in the copy. Only an arm64 compiler reads the line, and the nightly
  runs its violations on x86-64, so the script builds that binary for
  arm64 and runs it under qemu-aarch64's max model.

--- old
    ct_wipe(s, offsetof(aead_state, ghash) + offsetof(ghash_state, powers) +
                   s->powers * sizeof(ghash_power));
--- new
    ct_wipe(s, offsetof(aead_state, ghash) + offsetof(ghash_state, powers));
